                                                "sense_id": "7c0c4945-c7f6-31df-8865-9b52747db113",
                                                "text": "Euclid devised a simple, beautiful proof showing that there is an infinite number of primes. But what of the twin primes? As far as you go on the number line, will there always be another set of twins?"
                                            }
